course: dictionary
lesson: 4021
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is right. The word gate is a good example. «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» Here a gate is a door in a fence that opens and closes.
explain: «She waited at gate 9 for the plane.» Gate 9 is not a door in a fence. At an airport, a gate is the place where you get on the plane. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: «Babylon had mighty walls and the blue-tiled Ishtar Gate.» Mighty walls and a famous ancient city tell you this gate is an entrance into a city. Gates can be entrances too, like the school gate, where children go in each morning.
fact: A gate is a door in a fence, hedge or wall that opens and closes.
fact: At an airport, a gate is the place where you get on the plane.
fact: A gate can also be an entrance, where people go in, such as at a stadium or a school.
fact: Phrases you may meet: «front gate», «school gate», «go through the gate».
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Always close farm gates behind you so animals cannot escape.» What is a farm gate? | A place where you get on a plane | *A door in a fence that opens and closes | A kind of farm animal | A tall tower with a bell
exercise: «She waited at gate 9 for the plane.» What does gate mean here? | A small hill | A door in a fence | *The place where you get on the plane | A hole dug in the ground
exercise: «Mum walked Ben to the school gate each morning.» Where did Mum walk Ben to? | *The school entrance | A busy road | The school hall | A farm field
test: «Babylon had mighty walls and the blue-tiled Ishtar Gate.» What does gate mean in this sentence? | A tiny bird | *A great entrance in a city wall | A kind of tile | A shop window
test: Tom says gate only means a farm door. Which sentence proves he is wrong? | Leave the hedge alone | Always close farm gates behind you | *Fans queued at the stadium gate before the match | The fence is painted white
exam: How can you work out which meaning of gate is right in a sentence? | Look only at the first word | Choose the first meaning you know | Guess at random | *Read the words around it and check your meaning still fits
